\frac{8+8\sqrt{x+h}-(8+8\sqrt{x})}{h} = \frac{8\sqrt{x+h}-8\sqrt{x}}{h} =\frac{(8\sqrt{x+h}-8\sqrt{x})(8\sqrt{x+h}+8\sqrt{x})}{h(8\sqrt{x+h}+8\sqrt{x})} 
= \frac{64\mathopen{}\left(x+h\right)-64x}{h(8\sqrt{x+h}+8\sqrt{x})} = \frac{64h}{h(8\sqrt{x+h}+8\sqrt{x})} = \frac{64h}{8 h(\sqrt{x+h}+\sqrt{x})} 
Finally, we can divide to get
=\frac{8}{\sqrt{x+h}+\sqrt{x}}
That means A=8, while B=C=1.

Lastly, we can use this to calculate:
f'(1)= \frac{8}{2\sqrt{1}}
f'(2)= \frac{8}{2\sqrt{2}}
f'(3)= \frac{8}{2\sqrt{3}}
